        "C0313"
      ],
      "decision": "Four native operations already moved to B in P14. Current object/map bindings confirm same provider. No additional eliminated-ID credit."
    }
  ],
  "originalEvidence": {
    "revision": "5c5b979ec08c17d3ca2eb70e8aad62d26515d01c",
    "procedure": "git show original nt_error thread creation, wait, CloseHandle and exit; nt_fdisk geometry/alignment/BPB query calls. Source signatures and handle producer inspected.",
    "errorABI": "ErrorDialogBoxThread is DWORD WINAPI(VOID*); selected OPENNT_HOST_CREATE_THREAD_ABI chooses WINAPI bridge, unlike nt_com cdecl bridge.",
    "closeBoundary": "compat conapi.h globally maps CloseHandle to MvdmCloseConsoleHandle; provider falls through to native CloseHandle when handle is not graphics identity. Thread handle provenance proves this caller needs no graphics close behavior, not that every caller can bypass it."
  },
